<title>BELGIUM: EU proposes 30,000-tonne U.S. malt barley import quota.</title>
<headline>EU proposes 30,000-tonne U.S. malt barley import quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission proposed on Wednesday opening a 30,000-tonne reduced tariff quota for imports of U.S. malting barley, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The quota, which is valid for the remainder of 1996, allows for the import of U.S. Malting barley at 50 percent of the full duty.</p>
<p>&quot;The proposal was adopted,&quot; the spokesman said adding that it would now be sent to the farm Council for endorsement.</p>
<p>The EU granted the concession to compensate U.S. exporters for the loss of Austrian, Swedish and Finnish markets after these countries joined the EU in 1995.</p>
<p>The EU's delay in implementing this concession is among farm trade disputes being discussed by Commission and U.S. officials in Brussels this week.</p>
</text>
